{#
  checksum/<name> pod-template annotation — the trigger a Deployment/DaemonSet needs to
  restart on content it mounts but `ansible.builtin.template` never rendered. A ConfigMap
  staged by `kubectl create configmap --from-file` (observability's Grafana dashboards are the
  one left) sits outside the manifests role's own render/apply cycle, so `manifests_render is changed`
  (roles/k8s/manifests/tasks/main.yml) never fires for it and the pod keeps running the code
  it started with. See "A config edit won't restart the pod (k3s)" in the repo CLAUDE.md.

  A role that instead embeds its file via `lookup('file'|'template', ...)` directly INTO a
  manifest listed in `manifests_files`/`manifests_secret_files` needs no annotation at all —
  the embed changes the rendered manifest's bytes, `manifests_render is changed` fires on its
  own, and the central rollout-restart covers it. Reach for this macro only for content that
  reaches the cluster some other way. autofix-bridge's templates/script-configmap.yaml.j2 is
  the worked example of the embed, and monitor-bridge's splits one per module to stay under
  the client-side apply's annotation cap.

  Two call shapes, matching the two ways a caller computes its value:

    checksum_annotation('name', value=<already-computed checksum>)
      Renders the value verbatim, `| default('unstaged')`. Use this when the value comes from
      a task or a rendered value — a `copy` register, a fact hashing several files together,
      observability's hash of a ConfigMap body — anything other than one file's raw bytes,
      so a role's own computation is preserved exactly rather than approximated by this
      macro's own hashing.

    checksum_annotation('name', path=<absolute path to one file>)
      Hashes the file's raw bytes inline: `lookup('file', path, rstrip=False) | hash('sha1')`.
      `rstrip=False` is load-bearing — the file lookup's default strips trailing whitespace,
      which would hash different bytes than the file on disk and diverge from a `copy` task's
      own (unstripped) checksum of the same file. No caller uses this mode, but it stays
      correct for a role that stages exactly one file.

  `unstaged` is the value every existing checksum/ annotation falls back to on a config-only
  run (`--skip-tags deploy`), a `--dry-run` validator render, or a register/fact that never
  ran — stable across all three so none of them rolls the pod. `path` mode falls back the
  same way through the same `| default('unstaged')`: `scripts/validate/k8s_manifests.py`'s
  offline `lookup('file', ...)` shim reads the checked-in role file directly (there is no
  `--dry-run` case where that file is absent), so its render always yields a real digest
  rather than the placeholder.

  Invoke at the annotations block's indent, e.g.:
      annotations:
        {{ checksum_annotation('config', value=observability_grafana_config | hash('sha1')) }}
#}
{% macro checksum_annotation(name, value=None, path=None) -%}
checksum/{{ name }}: "{{ (value if path is none else (lookup('file', path, rstrip=False) | hash('sha1'))) | default('unstaged') }}"
{%- endmacro %}
